From: Herman Brule <brule.herman@confiared.com>
Subject: mips: -mfix-rlx, keep a three-operand mul out of branch delay slots

On the Realtek RLX (Lexra) Taroko core a branch whose delay slot holds
`mul rd,rs,rt`, rd being a register the branch reads, decides on the mul
result: `bnez $8; mul $8,a,b` branched wrong 100000/100000 (RTL9602C,
2026-10-03), while mflo/mfhi/addu/lw in the same slot were 0/100000.

--- a/gcc/config/mips/mips.opt
+++ b/gcc/config/mips/mips.opt
@@ -190,6 +190,10 @@
 Target Mask(FIX_R5900)
 Work around the R5900 short loop erratum.
 
+mfix-rlx
+Target Var(TARGET_FIX_RLX)
+Work around the Realtek RLX (Lexra) erratum: a branch whose delay slot holds a three-operand mul that writes a register the branch reads decides on the mul's result.
+
 mfix-rm7000
 Target Var(TARGET_FIX_RM7000)
 Work around certain RM7000 errata.
--- a/gcc/config/mips/mips.md
+++ b/gcc/config/mips/mips.md
@@ -775,7 +775,9 @@
 (define_attr "can_delay" "no,yes"
   (if_then_else (and (eq_attr "type" "!branch,call,jump,simd_branch")
 		     (eq_attr "hazard" "none")
-		     (match_test "get_attr_insn_count (insn) == 1"))
+		     (match_test "get_attr_insn_count (insn) == 1")
+		     (not (and (eq_attr "type" "imul3,imul3nc")
+			       (match_test "TARGET_FIX_RLX"))))
 		(const_string "yes")
 		(const_string "no")))
 
